  "verbalization": "Caffeine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Allergic Rhinitis through a chain of indications that ultimately converge on Potassium Iodide and then on Allergic Rhinitis. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence streams, each linking Caffeine to a different condition that ultimately leads to Allergic Rhinitis. The presence of Potassium Iodide as a common intermediate in all three paths suggests a potential mechanistic role, though the exact nature of this role remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible link between Caffeine and allergic inflammation, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise mechanism by which Caffeine influences the development of Allergic Rhinitis.",
